55,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B sounds appealing because it removes the ""price per switch"" anxiety, though we'd still have a year-end settle.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the simplest for the person doing the math, but it doesn't solve the fairness issue Jonathan mentioned.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C is the only one that actually addresses the room differences, even if it's expensive to set up.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I'm wary of Option C's cost. Option B provides more predictability for the monthly budget, which we clearly need.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I like Option A because it's easy, but I'm worried it will still lead to ""who uses more"" arguments.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, would you be okay with B if we agreed on a fair seasonal average?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, if we go with B, who handles the year-end reconciliation? That sounds like a huge task.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, B is better than A, but it doesn't stop the person in the cold room from paying for the person in the warm room.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, we could split the admin task or use a simple spreadsheet. The priority is stopping the ""second rent"" feeling in winter.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
