65,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'll vote for B. It balances the budget and the atmosphere of the house.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Mio,,I can't support C because of the admin and the cost. I'll vote for A to keep it simple.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I have to vote for C. The usage gap is too wide to ignore.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I'll vote for B. It's the most rational way to handle the volatility without spending a fortune on meters.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'll vote for B too. I just want the tension to go away.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
